Subject: src/liblzma/api/lzma.h: on OpenVMS, the library's /NAMES and flat subheaders

liblzma is compiled with /NAMES=(AS_IS,SHORTENED), as the OpenVMS family
of ports is: names keep their case, and those longer than 31 characters
are shortened the same way everywhere.  A program compiled with VSI C's
default /NAMES=UPPERCASE would look for LZMA_CODE and not find lzma_code.
Declare the API under #pragma names as_is, shortened on VMS, so programs
compiled with any /NAMES link with the library (as vms-zlib and vms-bzip2
do).

lzma.h includes its subheaders as "lzma/version.h" etc.  VSI C does not
find a quoted include with a directory part relative to a VMS include
directory (/INCLUDE=XZ$ROOT:[INCLUDE]), nor as "[.lzma]version.h".  On VMS
include them by flat names, lzma_version.h etc., which tools/prepare.sh
copies next to lzma.h and the kit installs beside it; the prefix keeps
generic names (index.h, block.h) apart from a program's own headers.

--- a/src/liblzma/api/lzma.h	2026-10-05 12:36:29.042507143 +0100
+++ b/src/liblzma/api/lzma.h	2026-10-05 12:41:32.522004994 +0100
@@ -280,6 +280,13 @@
  * Subheaders *
  **************/
 
+#ifdef __VMS
+/* The library is compiled with /NAMES=(AS_IS,SHORTENED); declare its API
+   so, whatever /NAMES the program is compiled with.  */
+#	pragma names save
+#	pragma names as_is, shortened
+#endif
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 extern "C" {
 #endif
